# Line endings that must not depend on who checked the tree out.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so a plain
# checkout rewrites text files to CRLF. That is harmless for sources, but fatal
# for anything a device or the Linux build container runs, and for patches that
# are applied as bytes:
#   - a CRLF shebang makes systemd report "status 203/EXEC" on the tablet;
#   - `git apply` / `patch` reject a CRLF patch file that was generated with LF.
# Pin those to LF so the working tree matches the index.
.gitattributes         text eol=lf
*.sh                   text eol=lf
*.py                   text eol=lf
*.patch                text eol=lf
*.diff                 text eol=lf
build.sh               text eol=lf
linux/userspace/**     text eol=lf
linux/bsp/**           text eol=lf
linux/configs/**       text eol=lf
